===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|nl|gas}}, {{coin|en|occ=chemist|Jan Baptist van Helmont|nocap=1|nocat=1}} in ''Ortus Medicinae''. Derived from {{der|en|grc|χάος|t=chasm, void, empty space}}; perhaps also inspired by {{m|nl|geest|t=breath, vapour, spirit}}. {{doublet|en|chaos}}. {{etydate|1648}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|+|++}}

# {{senseid|en|Q11432}} {{lb|en|uncountable|physical chemistry}} [[matter|Matter]] in an intermediate state between [[liquid]] and [[plasma]] that can be contained only if it is fully surrounded by a [[solid]] (or in a [[bubble]] of [[liquid]], or held together by gravitational pull); it can [[condense]] into a liquid, or can (rarely) become a [[solid]] directly by [[deposition]].
#: {{syn|en|vapor|vapour}}
#: {{ux|en|A lot of '''gas''' had escaped from the cylinder.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2013|month=July–August|author=Lee S. Langston|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=The Adaptable Gas Turbine|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/the-adaptable-gas-turbine|passage=Turbines have been around for a long time—windmills and water wheels are early examples. The name comes from the Latin ''turbo'', meaning ''vortex'', and thus the defining property of a turbine is that a fluid or '''gas''' turns the blades of a rotor, which is attached to a shaft that can perform useful work.|accessdate=12 September 2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130907101447/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/the-adaptable-gas-turbine|archivedate=7 September 2013}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} A flammable gaseous [[hydrocarbon]] or hydrocarbon mixture used as a fuel, e.g. for cooking, heating, electricity generation or as a fuel in internal combustion engines in vehicles, especially [[natural gas]].
##: {{ux|en|'''Gas'''-fired power stations have largely replaced coal-burning ones.}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable|military}} {{cap|poison gas}}.
##: {{ux|en|The artillery fired '''gas''' shells into the enemy trenches.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|physical chemistry}} A chemical [[element]] or [[compound]] in such a state.
#: {{ux|en|The atmosphere is made up of a number of different '''gases'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[hob]] on a gas [[cooker]].
#: {{ux|en|She turned the '''gas''' on, put the potatoes on, then lit the oven.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{cap|methane}} or other waste gases trapped in one's belly as a result of the digestive process; [[flatus]].
#: {{syn|en|wind}}
#: {{ux|en|My tummy hurts so bad – I have '''gas'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2008|author=Nicholas Drayson|title=A Guide to the Birds of East Africa|page=72|passage=But anyone with that many large brown birds aroost in his cranium and that much '''gas''' in his bottom was clearly not a well person.}}
# {{lb|en|business|often|attributive}} The [[supply]] of [[natural gas]], as a [[utility]].
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} A [[humorous]] or [[entertaining]] [[event]], [[person]]{{,}} or [[thing]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=Show Magazine|month=May|year=1963|title=A Bunny's Tale|author=w:Gloria Steinem|url=http://sites.dlib.nyu.edu/undercover/sites/dlib.nyu.edu.undercover/files/documents/uploads/editors/Show-A%20Bunny%27s%20Tale-Part%20One-May%201963.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20171004041757/http://sites.dlib.nyu.edu/undercover/sites/dlib.nyu.edu.undercover/files/documents/uploads/editors/Show-A%20Bunny's%20Tale-Part%20One-May%201963.pdf|archivedate=2017-10-04|passage=Two more girls came in, one in bright pink stretch pants and the other in purple. “Man this place is a '''gas''',” said pink.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1971|author=w:Marc Bolan|title=Life's a Gas|artist=T. Rex|album=Electric Warrior|passage=No it really doesn't matter at all / Life's a '''gas''' / I hope it's going to last}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=1973-03-01|artist=w:Pink Floyd|album=The Dark Side of the Moon|track=6|title=Money|url=https://genius.com/Pink-floyd-money-lyrics|passage=Money, it's a '''gas'''. Grab that cash with both hands and make a stash.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1978|artist={{w|Blondie (band)|Blondie}}|title={{w|Heart of Glass (song)|Heart of Glass}}|album=w:Parallel Lines|passage=Once I had a love and it was a '''gas''' / Soon turned out had a heart of glass}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Belsen Was a Gas|artist=Sex Pistols|year=1979|album=[[w:The Great Rock 'n' Roll Swindle (album)|The Great Rock ‛n’ Roll Swindle]]|passage=Be a man, Be a man / Belsen was a '''gas''' / Be a man, kill someone}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2011-10-11|title=Jumping Jack Flash (Live 1973)|artist=w:The Rolling Stones|album=Brussels Affair (Live 1973)|track=14|url=https://genius.com/The-rolling-stones-jumping-jack-flash-live-1973-lyrics|passage=One two! I was born in a cross-fire hurricane. And I howled at the maw in the drivin' rain. But it's all right now, in fact, it's a '''gas'''. But it's all right. I'm Jumpin' Jack Flash. It's a '''gas''', '''gas''', '''gas'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[frothy|Frothy]] or [[boastful]] [[talk]]; [[chatter]].
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2017-07-01|title=About That|artist=Soph Aspin; Millie B|text=Bang, little boy, stop with the '''gas''' / Little T, man he chats up his ass}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[fastball]].
#: {{ux|en|The closer threw him nothing but '''gas'''.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine|colloquial}} [[arterial blood gas|Arterial]] or [[venous]] [[blood]] gas.

